-- ss 10-14: 18 years, 70% of 987.65 = 691.355, to the nearest 10 cents 691.40; 15 years, 40% = 395.06, so 395.10;
-- 950 / 38 = 25.00 an hour; a casual adds 25%, 31.25; with a 30% loading by order, 32.50.
#ASSERT `What is my minimum weekly rate of pay` `as the employee` FALSE 25 FALSE 987.65 0 EQUALS amount 987.65
#ASSERT `What is my minimum weekly rate of pay` `as the employee` FALSE 18 FALSE 987.65 0 EQUALS amount 691.4
#ASSERT `What is my minimum weekly rate of pay` `as the employee` FALSE 15 FALSE 987.65 0 EQUALS amount 395.1
#ASSERT `What is my minimum weekly rate of pay` `as the employee` FALSE 19 TRUE 987.65 600 EQUALS amount 600
#ASSERT `What is my minimum weekly rate of pay` `as the employee` FALSE 20 FALSE 987.65 0 EQUALS amount (`What is my minimum weekly rate` 20 FALSE 987.65 0)
#ASSERT `What is my minimum hourly rate of pay` `as the employee` FALSE 950 FALSE 0 EQUALS amount 25
#ASSERT `What is my minimum hourly rate of pay` `as the employee` FALSE 950 TRUE 0 EQUALS amount 31.25
#ASSERT `What is my minimum hourly rate of pay` `as the employee` FALSE 950 TRUE 30 EQUALS amount 32.5
#ASSERT `What is my minimum hourly rate of pay` `as the employee` FALSE 987.65 TRUE 0 EQUALS amount (`What is my minimum hourly rate` 987.65 TRUE 0)

